:'''Mydei:''' Sadly, he has lost his voice now. If only the Chrysos Heirs could benefit from his wisdom&mdash;
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' M&mdash;Mydeimos...
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' Crown... prince?
:What's that sound!?
:He... He speaks!
:'''Mydei:''' ...Leo?
:'''Mydei:''' After all these years, you're still awake?
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' M&mdash;Mydeimos...
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' I could never... forget your voice. I've been waiting for this moment... all along.
:'''Mydei:''' Please, teacher, share your wise counsel with me!
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' Crown prince... Castrum Kremnos has lost everything &mdash; its people, traditions... and most importantly, its glory.
:'''Mydei:''' To survive, our people have migrated, and our traditions have faded with time. But glory? Even though it has vanished into the mist and its walls have crumbled, Castrum Kremnos has never forsaken the glory of its warriors. Why say otherwise?
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' Our god has completely lost their sanity. No longer a revered symbol of war, they have fallen and are now plotting an evil scheme...
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' I urge you, Mydeimos, to put an end to their endless suffering. Allow them to die as a warrior! They must... go with honor...
:'''Chryseus Leo:''' ...
:'''Mydei:''' Teacher?
:'''Mydei:''' Teacher, answer me! As your crown prince, I command you&mdash;
:'''Phainon:''' ...Mydei.
:'''Phainon:''' Let him rest. He must be exhausted.
:'''Mydei:''' ...
:'''Mydei:''' ...Perhaps those were just the delirious words of a dying lion. I shouldn't overthink it. Let's keep going.
:'''Phainon:''' Hold on. This is the slate that I mentioned earlier. We couldn't decipher it.
:'''Phainon:''' Maybe it's connected to the scheme the old lion mentioned.
:'''Mydei:''' Hand it to me.
:'''Mydei:''' No... {{Rubi|Nikador|Strife Titan}} would never...
:'''Phainon:''' That explains the surprise attack on Okhema. I didn't think that the mad Titan could have orchestrated it...
:'''Mydei:''' Okhema is on the brink of destruction. Someone needs to go back and rescue them.
:'''Phainon:''' ...
:'''Phainon:''' N&mdash;No, we need to press on and finish our mission.
:'''Mydei:''' Are you blinded by glory? As I said before, victory only lies in assembling a full-fledged army.
:'''Phainon:''' We're just one step away from {{Rubi|Nikador|Strife Titan}}. Defeat the source of the evil, and the threat will vanish on its own.
:'''Phainon:''' Just like that decisive strike, there is no turning back for us. {{Rubi|Nikador|Strife Titan}} could drive Okhema to the brink of ruin, but we can do the same to them.
:'''Phainon:''' Besides, I have faith in Aglaea and Tribbie. With two demigods and our allies watching over Okhema, they should be more than capable of protecting the holy city.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Dan Heng is there too.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We can't let our efforts go to waste.
:'''Mydei:''' ...
:{{tx}}
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location="Strife Ruins" Castrum Kremnos|update|Through Chryseus Leo, (Trailblazer) and the party learned that the maddened Nikador is planning a devastating attack on Okhema. With events taking this dire turn, their only option is to press forward and eliminate the source of this malevolence.}}
